    "title": "What time is UCLA vs South Carolina national championship today? Start time, location, TV Channel",
    "text": "Updated April 5, 2026, 8:37 p.m. ETWhat started with 68 teams a few weeks ago is down to just two teams. The women's NCAA Tournament is all set to crown a national champion as No. 1 seed UCLA looks to halt No. 1 seed South Carolina's quest for a fourth title since 2017.The title game tips off airs live on ABC and ESPN at 3:30 p.m. ET on Sunday, April 5.Here's everything you need to know to tune in for the clash between the Gamecocks and Bruins.USA TODAY Sports has a team of journalists covering women's March Madness to keep you up to date with every point scored, rebound grabbed and game won in the 68-team tournament.What time is South Carolina vs UCLA national championship game?No. 1 UCLA vs No. 1 South Carolina tips off at 3:30 PM (ET) on Sunday, April 05 from Mortgage Matchup Center (Phoenix, Arizona).How to watch South Carolina vs UCLA national championship gameMatchup : No. 1 South Carolina Gamecocks vs. No. 1 UCLA BruinsDate: Sunday, April 05Time: 3:30 PM (ET)Venue: Mortgage Matchup CenterLocation: Phoenix, ArizonaTV: ABCStreaming: Fubo Watch the NCAA Tournament all March long with FuboSouth Carolina March Madness resultsRound of 62: def No. 16 Southern, 103-34Round of 32: def No. 9 USC, 101-61Sweet 16: def No. 4 Oklahoma, 94-68Elite Eight: def. No. 3 TCU, 78-52Final Four: def No. 1 UConn, 62-48UCLA March Madness resultsRound of 62: def No. 16 CA Baptist, 96-43Round of 32: def No. 8 Oklahoma St., 87-68Sweet 16: def. No. 4 Minnesota, 80-56Elite Eight: def No. 3 Duke, 70-58Final Four: def No. 1 Texas, 51-44Women's March Madness schedule todaySee the schedule, live scores and results for all of Sunday's NCAA Tournament action here.2026 Women's NCAA Tournament full scheduleMarch 18-19: First FourMarch 20-21: First RoundMarch 22-23: Second RoundMarch 27-28: Sweet 16March 29-30: Elite 8April 3: Final FourApril 5: National ChampionshipOur editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, howe